ef 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3df2c088-75da-58f8-942c-5d4b3a14d502" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061618 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "419036f6-f9dd-5b25-a7a0-84c4a9c291ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186061619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e6555da-0526-5464-be80-e4fe3bd7facd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064045 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3736" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064045 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the global extrema of $f(x) = 2x - x^2$  on the interval $[-1,4].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064045 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69180c3b-7c26-5e5f-8d7a-42aed98431bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064045 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=2x-x^2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 2-2x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n2-2x = 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad x=1.\n$$\n\nThe critical points are $x=1$ and the endpoints $x=-1,4$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2(-1)-(-1)^{2}=-3 \\\\ f(1) & =2(1)-(1)^{2}=1 \\\\ f(4) & =2(4)-(4)^{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(1)=1,$ so the global maximum value is $1.$\n\n- The least value is $f(4)=-8,$ so the global minimum value is $-8.$\n\n![](images/c2/c277beb3423cc80d3ac2a001ac1063059b645c65fc8cb77978050f3831274b31.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064046 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3737" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064046 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the global maximum and minimum values for the function $f(x) = x^4 - 6 x^2$ on the closed interval $[-1, 3].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064046 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0f47cd2-ea8f-5278-ab67-46ecd65d2f4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064046 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x^4 - 6x^2,$ we get\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 4x^3 - 12x,\n$$\n\nand solving $f'(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x = -\\sqrt 3 \\approx -1.73$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,3]$, we ignore this point.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=0,\\sqrt{3}$ and the endpoints $x=-1,3$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\nFinally, we evaluate $f$ at the critical points:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tf(-1) \t& = (-1)^4 - 6(-1)^2 = -5\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(0) \t\t& = (0)^4 - 6(0)^2 = 0\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(\\sqrt 3) \t& = (\\sqrt 3)^4 - 6(\\sqrt 3)^2 = -9\\[5pt]\n \t\tf(3) \t\t& = (3)^4 - 6(3)^2 = 27 \\\t\t\n \t\t}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the global maximum is $27$ and the global minimum is $-9.$\n\n![](images/74/74ce5114dbc93035b0be078be12149cced66ce881dfbc37768ed9febcdfcba87.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186288024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064163 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1039 "Discarding Stationary Points of a Function on a Given Interval" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064164 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2106ea68-f48f-5372-87c0-fa8126509655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186064996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1045 "The Candidates Test" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186064994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1050 840.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186064451 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b309af6c-4786-5404-a3b4-0a5fc0d4a4ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064572 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186061614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064572 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064572 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x}$ on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2} \\le x \\le 2$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064572 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2435a5d9-0223-53db-acdd-e3c8030d82a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064572 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064994 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186064995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064994 #edb/ref 1061 12797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064994 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b5f6fdc-d0a8-5c91-a879-4f798a936a36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064994 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064995 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186064996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064995 #edb/ref 1061 12798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064995 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8149edd7-e4fe-579d-804f-4e9bf9911f55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064995 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064996 #edb/ref 1061 12799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064996 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5743e9b2-be38-579c-8843-93e55b3e92f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064996 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065348 #edb/ref 1064 "We know how to use the first derivative test to find the local extrema of a continuous function. But how do we find the global extrema of a continuous function on a closed interval $[a,b]?$\n\nWe apply the **candidates test**, which consists of the following three steps.\n\n**Step 1**:  Find all of the critical points. The critical points are our \"candidates.\"\n\n- If the function is defined on a closed interval $[a,b],$ then we must remember to include the endpoints as well.\n\n- If the function is defined on an open interval $(a,b),$ then we do not include the endpoints.\n\n**Step 2**: Determine the value of the function at each of the critical points.\n\n**Step 3**: Compare all the values of $f$ found in step $2.$ The greatest of these values is the global maximum value, and the least is the global minimum value." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065348 #edb/ref 1065 2667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065348 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e714b234-f163-5ae5-a064-6bef2d3b9fc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065348 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290805 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290805 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290805 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2a8313dd-5fdd-5c81-a1b5-48c8c4a34af4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290842 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33ed80ac-0b34-5d04-b4be-e2a0347c210b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290917 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290917 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290917 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45594262-3efe-57c7-b5b9-bfdbc6564c55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290940 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290940 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290940 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a244d28-9365-55e7-81e4-fdf02c2a2c60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291099 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291099 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c95327d-f3a6-5aaa-8c47-7b4e3d402e29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291136 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291136 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291136 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7620126f-9b05-57e1-83c0-abc96aed6552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291138 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "76c4c7f4-f5c8-5499-94aa-d57c71cb7050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291169 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291169 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291169 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7eb07632-b195-5870-b2a7-66c1d64cb5d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291368 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291368 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291368 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a844a83e-0aac-539f-89a3-bca1ef965168" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291701 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291701 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291701 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fba97015-0947-55e9-a31d-e68b17721999" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292209 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "966e70db-9154-5f74-a132-3c4d2bdeac39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f1d95fed-6abb-5898-9ccd-fc77f7d79a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2690" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+9x+3,$ on the closed interval $-4\\le x\\le -2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $3$\n- The global minimum value is $1$\n- The global minimum value is $-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bea0a781-9898-5e25-a447-5b87446089a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292684 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+9x+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}+12x+9 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}+4x+3) \\\\  & =3(x+1)(x+3),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n3(x+1)(x+3)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3,\\,-1.\n$$\n\nSince $x=-1$ does not belong to the interval $[-4,-2]$, the critical points are $x=-3$ and the endpoints $x=-4,-2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =(-4)^{3}+6(-4)^{2}+9(-4)+3=-1 \\\\ f(-3) & =(-3)^{3}+6(-3)^{2}+9(-3)+3=3 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{3}+6(-2)^{2}+9(-2)+3=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=3,$ so the global maximum is $3.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-4)=-1,$ so the global minimum is $-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"\n\n![](images/fa/fa85119166ca325f9925ddd03a578fb5daae463c59c3b7b9f7ac0f6464a30241.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1071 "Find  the global minimum value of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8383b31-3ef6-56e1-8528-1bcdbd1b3b84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{2}(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}-8(-1)^{3}+3=14 \\\\ f(0) & =3(0)^{4}-8(0)^{3}+3=3 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}-8(1)^{3}+3=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=14,$ so the global maximum is $14.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=-2,$ so the global minimum is $-2.$\n\n![](images/9a/9ac7f0c0e28532c897e1c89a35e9c027f614fee40b4b94362a6c5cb012c8a7f6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315928 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315928 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315928 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9151074f-2d08-535c-a8e8-72d9cbef933e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316922 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316922 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316922 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316922 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316922 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1a59685-a019-5aa4-aeb6-c0eab15154c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344373" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1071 "The global maximum value of the function $f(x)=-x+4$ on the closed interval $1\\le x\\le 5$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50b35122-a792-5902-a8d9-65288095b044" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317496 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=-x+4,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-1.\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all real values of $x.$ So there is no solution for ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$\n\nSo, the only critical points are the endpoints $x=1,5$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-(1)+4=3 \\\\ f(5) & =-(5)+4=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(1)=3,$ so the global maximum is $3.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(5)=-1,$ so the global minimum is $-1.$\n\n![](images/b6/b66a275ad0f733f9b7a715cacc87e47ab42200def67a3a7f5a5e577ba067a1c3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
